From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dusk Player <dusk@localhost>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] contrib/ffmpeg: re-enable TrueHD/MLP decoding on
 iOS/tvOS

VLCKit's patch 0007 disables ffmpeg's mlp decoder, demuxer and parser on
iOS "to be in compliance with the App Store ToS" (Dolby licensing; AC-3 /
E-AC-3 are decoded through Apple's licensed AudioToolbox instead, but no
system decoder exists for TrueHD). Because ffmpeg's truehd decoder depends
on the mlp parser, that block removes TrueHD decoding entirely: libvlc
fails with "Codec `mlpa' (TrueHD Audio) is not supported" and Bluray-remux
default tracks cannot be played.

Dropping the block restores the stock ffmpeg behaviour (truehd and mlp
decoders are enabled by default), so TrueHD/Atmos tracks decode to PCM.

NOTE: applying this patch is a deliberate licensing / App Store decision
by the app maintainer, not a build default. After rebuilding the
frameworks with this patch, also remove the TrueHD/MLP fourccs from
`VLCKitEngine.undecodableAudioFourCCs` so the tracks become selectable
again.
---
 contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak b/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
--- a/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/ffmpeg/rules.mak
@@ -41,13 +41,7 @@
 ifdef HAVE_DARWIN_OS
 FFMPEGCONF += \
 	--disable-securetransport
-ifdef HAVE_IOS
-FFMPEGCONF += \
-	--disable-decoder=mlp \
-	--disable-demuxer=mlp \
-	--disable-parser=mlp
 endif
-endif
 
 ifdef ENABLE_PDB
 FFMPEGCONF += --ln_s=false
